// Bind truth strictly to raw order cashflow; completely disregard platform-reported conversions
orders = ingest_first_party_unmodeled_sales_ledger()

// Continuous holdouts leak and MMM stationarity is broken by opaque bidding updates
for channel in [pmax, meta_asc]:
  // Force causal variance via randomized, orthogonal spend pulsing rather than steady-state spend
  pulse_schedule = generate_short_window_spend_shocks(channel, duration_days=3)
  enforce_strict_spend_limits(channel, pulse_schedule)

  // Measure instantaneous business-level impulse response, bypassing platform pixels entirely
  observed_cash_delta = isolate_aggregate_revenue_shift(orders, pulse_schedule)

  // Disagree with pure MMM: explicitly penalize the platform when pullback exposes internal cannibalization
  if direct_and_organic_inverts(pulse_schedule):
    penalize_attribution(channel, metric=branded_demand_harvesting)

// Output wide operational spend corridors rather than false-precision point estimates
return derive_min_max_budget_bounds(observed_cash_delta, confidence_decay='rapid')

Stop auditing ghosts;
spend the year on switchbacks —
truth is a rate, not reads.

Hush now, start with outcomes, deduped, timely, clean;
Seed tiny random holdbacks only where they can be seen.

Don’t crown one grand MMM and sing its answer true;
Use sparse tests to falsify what models claim they do.

When agents shift their bidding, mark each regime anew;
Pool only stable windows, bound what data cannot view.

Score vendors blind on shared trials, bring failures into light;
Yet walls that hide the dose still bar us from causal sight.
